  "correction_rules": [
    "Reduce forecast overshoots following sharp upward spikes in price, especially when sentiment is neutral or negative.",
    "Adjust forecasts downward if recent history shows persistent mean reversion toward lower levels, particularly after sustained high peaks.",
    "Apply a bias correction factor when sentiment history includes multiple negative entries (e.g., >2 consecutive negative sentiment values), indicating downward pressure.",
    "Smooth out forecast volatility when sentiment is flat (0.00) over recent days, suggesting lack of directional momentum.",
    "Increase downward adjustment magnitude if true outcomes consistently lag behind forecasts in early periods (e.g., first 5–10 days of forecast horizon).",
    "When sentiment turns positive (e.g., >0.00) after a negative streak, gradually increase forecast optimism but cap it at 10–15% above recent low to avoid overcorrection."
  ]
